+{# The thread is unconditional — it is narrative, and every scaffold surface has
+   something to say. The input field is not: `cm.field` hardcodes
+   action="{{ c.composerAction }}" with no guard of its own, so a facade that
+   sets no action renders `action=""`, which posts the page to itself. A surface
+   with no mutation (scaffold.run is a read receipt over a frozen run) must
+   render no field rather than a field wired to nowhere. Gating on the action
+   makes `action=""` structurally unreachable here.
+
+   This gate is deliberately NOT in shared widgets/composer.html: intake and
+   design import that file too, and it would be a no-op for them while changing
+   a file their owners depend on.
+
+   Known cost: a facade that forgets composerAction now loses its composer
+   silently instead of visibly breaking. The check that catches the other half
+   (action set, nobody routed it — a rendered-markup sweep, since the selftest
+   reads template source where this attribute is never a literal) is written up
+   in docs/plans/composer-action-integrity.md. That defect is live on
+   /scaffold today: action="/scaffold/messages" renders, POST returns 404. #}
 {% macro composerPanel(c) %}
 {% set CP = { eyebrow: c.stageEyebrow, chips: c.chips } %}
 {{ cp.open(CP) }}
   {{ thread(c) }}
-  {{ cm.field(c) }}
+  {% if c.composerAction %}{{ cm.field(c) }}{% endif %}
 {{ cp.close(CP) }}
 {% endmacro %}
 
